# This file still labels path ownership in the GitHub UI, but it is NOT a
# merge gate -- corrected 2026-08-19 (E-012), found while merging this repo's
# first PR. GitHub refuses to let a PR author approve their own PR ("Review
# Can not approve your own pull request"), and this ruleset's bypass_actors is
# empty (E-010: personal account, no org), so even --admin can't override it
# either. A required-review rule nobody can ever satisfy is a lockout, not
# security -- "Require review from Code Owners" was removed from the main
# ruleset. Single owner, personal repo, no second reviewer identity (E-005).
# Real enforcement is required status checks (still fully real, see
# .github/workflows/) plus docs/runbooks/self-review-protocol.md's Tier-2
# scrutiny on the paths below -- a personal commitment, not a GitHub feature.

* @microbrewerGM

# THE critical protection: agent constraints and CI cannot self-modify
/.claude/                            @microbrewerGM
/.github/                            @microbrewerGM

# Rights: the manifest and the workflow that checks it are owned separately
# on purpose. data-rights must not be able to weaken its own gate.
/catalog/rights/                     @microbrewerGM
/.github/workflows/rights-gate.yml   @microbrewerGM

# Infra: laptop review, self-review protocol Tier 2
/infra/                              @microbrewerGM

# Security surface: self-review protocol Tier 2
/worker/src/security/                @microbrewerGM

# Domain paths
/pipeline/                           @microbrewerGM
/worker/                             @microbrewerGM
/catalog/                            @microbrewerGM
/tests/baselines/                    @microbrewerGM
